1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,755
On Monday, there's a list on your fridge.

2
00:00:03,775 --> 00:00:04,995
Five names.

3
00:00:05,015 --> 00:00:07,360
Every friendship you ever let break.

4
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:09,960
Fix one, and the name turns gold.

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:12,000
Don't, and on Sunday at midnight, they're

6
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:12,845
gone.

7
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:14,240
Not dead.

8
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:15,465
Just gone.

9
00:00:15,485 --> 00:00:16,915
You'll pass them in the street, and

10
00:00:16,935 --> 00:00:19,012
neither of you will know why you looked.

11
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:21,151
You have seven days.

12
00:00:24,201 --> 00:00:26,381
The first four are easy to guess.

13
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,112
The fifth one makes you laugh.

14
00:00:28,132 --> 00:00:28,512
Theo?

15
00:00:28,532 --> 00:00:29,412
He lives here.

16
00:00:29,432 --> 00:00:30,897
He eats my cereal.

17
00:00:31,047 --> 00:00:33,077
You decide the list is broken.

18
00:00:33,097 --> 00:00:34,677
Lists can be broken.

19
00:00:34,697 --> 00:00:36,577
You put a magnet over his name and go

20
00:00:36,597 --> 00:00:37,418
to work.

21
00:00:38,408 --> 00:00:38,690
Jo.

22
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:41,781
In 2019 he sent you a very long message.

23
00:00:41,801 --> 00:00:44,270
You meant to answer it properly.

24
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:45,661
You never did.

25
00:00:45,681 --> 00:00:46,511
You never answered.

26
00:00:46,531 --> 00:00:47,847
Not even a thumbs up.

27
00:00:47,867 --> 00:00:48,572
I know.

28
00:00:48,592 --> 00:00:49,965
It was a long message.

29
00:00:49,985 --> 00:00:51,333
It was about my dad.

30
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:52,463
I'm sorry.

31
00:00:52,483 --> 00:00:53,458
I didn't know.

32
00:00:53,478 --> 00:00:54,548
You didn't ask.

33
00:00:55,298 --> 00:00:56,053
He's right.

34
00:00:56,073 --> 00:00:57,053
You didn't.

35
00:00:57,073 --> 00:00:59,098
You were busy, and then you were embarrassed

36
00:00:59,118 --> 00:01:01,293
about being busy, and then it was four

37
00:01:01,313 --> 00:01:02,101
years.

38
00:01:02,121 --> 00:01:03,011
How is he?

39
00:01:03,031 --> 00:01:03,928
Your dad.

40
00:01:03,948 --> 00:01:04,228
Better.

41
00:01:04,248 --> 00:01:05,709
Do you actually want to know?

42
00:01:05,729 --> 00:01:07,517
I actually want to know.

43
00:01:08,567 --> 00:01:09,307
You ask.

44
00:01:09,327 --> 00:01:10,757
He talks for an hour.

45
00:01:10,777 --> 00:01:12,524
You don't check your phone once.

46
00:01:13,514 --> 00:01:13,898
Sam.

47
00:01:13,918 --> 00:01:17,046
You still have her jacket from a party

48
00:01:17,066 --> 00:01:18,032
in 2017.

49
00:01:18,052 --> 00:01:19,421
You've had it seven years.

50
00:01:19,441 --> 00:01:21,045
It's a really good jacket.

51
00:01:21,065 --> 00:01:22,670
Bring it to football on Thursday.

52
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:23,621
You're in goal.

53
00:01:23,771 --> 00:01:25,376
You let in nine goals.

54
00:01:25,396 --> 00:01:28,051
Sam laughs so hard she has to sit down.

55
00:01:28,071 --> 00:01:28,850
Gold.

56
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:30,400
Same time next week?

57
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:32,296
You can be worse in a different position.

58
00:01:32,446 --> 00:01:33,801
Two names down.

59
00:01:33,821 --> 00:01:34,901
Three to go.

60
00:01:34,921 --> 00:01:36,401
You start to think this is going to

61
00:01:36,421 --> 00:01:37,348
be easy.

62
00:01:38,998 --> 00:01:39,353
Mr.

63
00:01:39,373 --> 00:01:39,963
Hale.

64
00:01:39,983 --> 00:01:41,163
Your old neighbour.

65
00:01:41,183 --> 00:01:42,948
You waved at the van, and you never

66
00:01:42,968 --> 00:01:43,701
visited.

67
00:01:43,721 --> 00:01:45,151
Well, look who it is!

68
00:01:45,171 --> 00:01:47,481
Come in, I've got eight kinds of biscuits

69
00:01:47,501 --> 00:01:48,917
and nobody to eat them.

70
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,822
You eat all eight kinds.

71
00:01:50,842 --> 00:01:53,497
He shows you his tomatoes, one by one.

72
00:01:53,517 --> 00:01:54,659
He has named them.

73
00:01:54,679 --> 00:01:56,209
That one's called Gerald.

74
00:01:56,229 --> 00:01:57,459
He's my best one.

75
00:01:57,479 --> 00:01:58,795
Don't tell the others.

76
00:01:58,945 --> 00:02:00,275
You stay for dinner.

77
00:02:00,295 --> 00:02:02,100
You miss the last train and sleep on

78
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,150
his sofa under a blanket that smells

79
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:05,350
of biscuits.

80
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:06,130
Gold.

81
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:07,500
Danny.

82
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,830
Your best friend when you were fourteen.

83
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:11,480
You moved schools, and you promised

84
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,905
to write, and you didn't.

85
00:02:12,925 --> 00:02:14,046
Not once.

86
00:02:14,066 --> 00:02:15,521
Danny doesn't pick up.

87
00:02:15,541 --> 00:02:16,406
Thursday.

88
00:02:16,426 --> 00:02:17,251
Friday.

89
00:02:17,271 --> 00:02:18,321
Saturday.

90
00:02:18,341 --> 00:02:20,624
On Saturday night, he texts back.

91
00:02:20,644 --> 00:02:21,694
I'm not ready.

92
00:02:21,759 --> 00:02:23,394
Maybe one day.

93
00:02:24,344 --> 00:02:26,049
The D stays white.

94
00:02:26,069 --> 00:02:27,724
You can't fix someone who doesn't want

95
00:02:27,744 --> 00:02:28,799
to be fixed.

96
00:02:28,819 --> 00:02:30,922
You can only leave the door open.

97
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,062
Whenever you're ready.

98
00:02:32,082 --> 00:02:33,140
I'll answer.

99
00:02:35,090 --> 00:02:35,790
Sunday.

100
00:02:35,845 --> 00:02:37,325
Six hours left.

101
00:02:37,345 --> 00:02:38,475
One name.

102
00:02:38,495 --> 00:02:39,465
Theo.

103
00:02:39,485 --> 00:02:41,640
You've fed him, housed him, said sorry

104
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:42,590
to him.

105
00:02:42,610 --> 00:02:44,440
But you realise you've never once asked

106
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,116
him a question you didn't already know

107
00:02:46,136 --> 00:02:47,233
the answer to.

108
00:02:47,253 --> 00:02:47,903
Theo.

109
00:02:47,923 --> 00:02:49,787
What's that game you play every night?

110
00:02:49,807 --> 00:02:50,963
You want to know?

111
00:02:50,983 --> 00:02:52,160
I want to play.

112
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,379
You'll be terrible.

113
00:02:53,399 --> 00:02:54,235
I know.

114
00:02:54,255 --> 00:02:55,730
You have to be the green one.

115
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:57,579
The green one always dies first.

116
00:02:57,599 --> 00:02:59,177
That feels personal.

117
00:03:00,227 --> 00:03:01,227
You're terrible.

118
00:03:01,247 --> 00:03:02,772
He teaches you anyway.

119
00:03:02,792 --> 00:03:03,897
He's patient.

120
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,584
You didn't know he was patient.

121
00:03:05,604 --> 00:03:07,251
You keep looking at the fridge.

122
00:03:07,271 --> 00:03:08,338
No, I don't.

123
00:03:08,358 --> 00:03:10,103
Is my name on that thing?

124
00:03:10,603 --> 00:03:11,108
It was.

125
00:03:11,128 --> 00:03:12,079
Under a magnet.

126
00:03:12,099 --> 00:03:12,754
Why?

127
00:03:12,774 --> 00:03:14,354
Because I've been your brother your

128
00:03:14,374 --> 00:03:15,604
whole life.

129
00:03:15,624 --> 00:03:17,670
I don't think I've ever been your friend.

130
00:03:18,270 --> 00:03:18,700
Okay.

131
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:18,925
Well.

132
00:03:18,945 --> 00:03:20,150
Friends don't let friends be the green

133
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:20,820
one.

134
00:03:20,845 --> 00:03:21,559
Swap.

135
00:03:22,609 --> 00:03:24,614
At two minutes to midnight, the last

136
00:03:24,634 --> 00:03:25,993
T turns gold.

137
00:03:26,683 --> 00:03:28,163
Four gold names.

138
00:03:28,183 --> 00:03:29,253
One white one.

139
00:03:29,273 --> 00:03:31,153
You leave the list on the fridge.

140
00:03:31,173 --> 00:03:33,122
Just in case Danny calls.

141
00:03:35,512 --> 00:03:37,598
Whose name would be on your list?
